sections.text:
In this Act, unless there is anything repugnant in the subject or context:
(a) 'Building' includes a house, outhouse, shed, hut, and any other such structure, whether of masonry, bricks, wood, mud, metal or any other material whatsoever, but does not include any building used for the purpose of carrying on any business or profession;
(d) 'Privileged person' means a person (i) who is not a proprietor, tenure-holder, under-tenure holder or a mahajan; and (ii) who, besides his homestead, holds no other land or holds any such land not exceeding one acre.

A privileged tenant shall be liable to be ejected from his homestead only on the following grounds, namely:
(a) that he has used the homestead for a purpose other than for residential purposes;
(b) that he has failed to pay the rent of the homestead for two consecutive years;
(c) that he has transferred his holding or any part thereof in contravention of the provisions of this Act.
